segments.source:
We can perform row operations to clear the entries above the nonzero diagonal entries:
                <me>
                  \mat{a_{11} \star, \star, \star;
                     0 a_{22} \star, \star; 0 0 0 \star; 0 0 0 a_{44}}
                  \;\xrightarrow{\phantom{MMM}}\;
                  \mat{a_{11} 0, \star, 0;
                     0 a_{22} \star, 0; 0 0 0 0; 0 0 0 a_{44}}
                </me>
                In the resulting matrix, the <m>i</m>th row is zero, so <m>\det(A) = 0</m> by the first part.

segments.translation:
행 연산을 수행하여 0이 아닌 대각성분 위에 있는 성분들을 소거할 수 있습니다: <me>
                  \mat{a_{11} \star, \star, \star;
                     0 a_{22} \star, \star; 0 0 0 \star; 0 0 0 a_{44}}
                  \;\xrightarrow{\phantom{MMM}}\;
                  \mat{a_{11} 0, \star, 0;
                     0 a_{22} \star, 0; 0 0 0 0; 0 0 0 a_{44}}
                </me> 그 결과로 얻은 행렬에서 <m>i</m>번째 행은 영행이므로, 첫 번째 부분에 의해 <m>\det(A) = 0</m>입니다.

segments.source:
Then <m>A</m> can be transformed to the identity matrix by scaling the diagonal entries and then doing row replacements:
                <me>
\begin{split} \amp\mat{a \star, \star; 0 b \star; 0 0 c}
    \;\xrightarrow{%
    \begin{minipage}{1.8cm}%
      \tiny\centering scale by\\$a\inv,b\inv,c\inv$%
    \end{minipage}}\;
    \mat{1 \star, \star; 0 1 \star; 0 0 1}
    \;\xrightarrow{%
    \begin{minipage}{1.6cm}%
      \tiny\centering row\\replacements%
    \end{minipage}}\;
    \mat{1 0 0; 0 1 0; 0 0 1} \\
    \amp
    \hbox to 2.1cm{\hss$\det=abc$\hss} \;\xleftarrow{\hbox to 1.8cm{\hss}}\;
    \hbox to 2.1cm{\hss$\det=1$\hss} \;\xleftarrow{\hbox to 1.6cm{\hss}}\;
    \hbox to 1.8cm{\hss$\det=1$}
\end{split}
                </me>
                Since <m>\det(I_n) = 1</m> and we scaled by the reciprocals of the diagonal entries, this implies <m>\det(A)</m> is the product of the diagonal entries.

segments.translation:
그러면 대각성분을 스케일링한 다음 행 대체를 하여 <m>A</m>를 단위행렬로 변환할 수 있습니다. <me>
\begin{split} \amp\mat{a \star, \star; 0 b \star; 0 0 c}
    \;\xrightarrow{%
    \begin{minipage}{1.8cm}%
      \tiny\centering scale by\\$a\inv,b\inv,c\inv$%
    \end{minipage}}\;
    \mat{1 \star, \star; 0 1 \star; 0 0 1}
    \;\xrightarrow{%
    \begin{minipage}{1.6cm}%
      \tiny\centering row\\replacements%
    \end{minipage}}\;
    \mat{1 0 0; 0 1 0; 0 0 1} \\
    \amp
    \hbox to 2.1cm{\hss$\det=abc$\hss} \;\xleftarrow{\hbox to 1.8cm{\hss}}\;
    \hbox to 2.1cm{\hss$\det=1$\hss} \;\xleftarrow{\hbox to 1.6cm{\hss}}\;
    \hbox to 1.8cm{\hss$\det=1$}
\end{split}
                </me> <m>\det(I_n) = 1</m>이고 대각성분의 역수로 스케일링하였으므로, 이로부터 <m>\det(A)</m>가 대각성분의 곱임을 알 수 있습니다.

기본행렬에는 행 대체, 행 스케일링, 행 교환에서 생기는 세 종류가 있습니다. <me>
            \begin{split}
               \mat{1 0 0;  0 1 0; 0 0 1} \xrightarrow{\parbox{2cm}{\tiny\centering$R_2 = R_2 - 2R_1$}}\amp
               \mat{1 0 0; -2 1 0; 0 0 1} \\
               \mat{1 0 0;  0 1 0; 0 0 1} \xrightarrow{\parbox{2cm}{\tiny\centering$R_1 = 3R_1$}}\amp
               \mat{3 0 0;  0 1 0; 0 0 1} \\
               \mat{1 0 0;  0 1 0; 0 0 1} \xrightarrow{\parbox{2cm}{\tiny\centering$R_1 \longleftrightarrow R_2$}}\amp
               \mat{0 1 0;  1 0 0; 0 0 1}
            \end{split}
          </me> 기본행렬의 중요한 성질은 다음 주장입니다.

segments.source:
Since left-multiplication by <m>E</m> does not change the determinant, we have <m>\det(ECB) = \det(CB)</m>, so
              <me>
                d(C') = \frac{\det(C'B)}{\det(B)}
                = \frac{\det(ECB)}{\det(B)}
                = \frac{\det(CB)}{\det(B)}
                = d(C).
              </me>

Since left-multiplication by <m>E</m> scales the determinant by a factor of <m>c</m>, we have <m>\det(ECB) = c\det(CB)</m>, so
              <me>
                d(C') = \frac{\det(C'B)}{\det(B)}
                = \frac{\det(ECB)}{\det(B)}
                = \frac{c\det(CB)}{\det(B)}
                = c\cdot d(C).
              </me>

Since left-multiplication by <m>E</m> negates the determinant, we have <m>\det(ECB) = -\det(CB)</m>, so
              <me>
                d(C') = \frac{\det(C'B)}{\det(B)}
                = \frac{\det(ECB)}{\det(B)}
                = \frac{-\det(CB)}{\det(B)}
                = -d(C).
              </me>

